<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bale</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bale is a region in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. In the fourteenth century it was one of the territories incorporated into the Christian Ethiopian state through the expansion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amda-seyon-i">Amda Seyon</a>. Control of Bale was part of the long contest between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> and Muslim sultanates to the east.</p></div>
